        <mxCell id="hardware-c97" value="&lt;b&gt;Why the budget matters&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;• A refit that adds two cameras and a digital menu board adds about 45 W: still inside 370 W.&lt;br&gt;• Keep each switch under about 80 % of its budget. Past 100 % it refuses or drops power, and port priority decides who loses: PIN pads and APs high, signage low.&lt;br&gt;• Check the AP datasheet: many Wi-Fi 6E and 7 models need 802.3bt for full function.&lt;br&gt;• Record each PoE device's class on its NetBox interface (PoE mode and type) and this table can be checked against NetBox." style="rounded=1;absoluteArcSize=1;arcSize=16;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#E2E8F0;strokeWidth=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=10;fontSize=10;fontColor=#334155;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontFamily=Inter;" vertex="1" parent="hardware-L4">
